---
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---
<section class="privacy-section" id="privacy"><div class="container-site">
  <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Private by default</p><h2>Your phone is home.<br />Sharing is your choice.</h2><p>No bank connection or mandatory account. Everyday money tracking works offline.</p></div>
  <div class="privacy-grid">
    <article class="panel local-panel"><span class="badge">Available now · Local</span><h3>Your personal garden</h3><p>Expenses, income, budgets, savings goals and custom people live in the app’s private storage.</p>
      <ol class="data-flow" aria-label="Local data flow"><li>Your financial records</li><li aria-hidden="true">↓</li><li>Your device</li><li aria-hidden="true">↓</li><li>Private app storage</li></ol>
      <p class="text-ink-muted">Exporting a backup or statement creates a file you control. Keep backups somewhere you trust. App lock controls access; it does not encrypt the stored records.</p>
      <p class="planned-note">In development: local SQLite storage with migration of existing records. Not yet in the published APK.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="panel" id="sharing"><span class="badge">Planned · Optional online</span><h3>A shared corner with friends</h3><p>Username sharing is planned for a future release. It is not available in the current download.</p>
      <ol class="sharing-steps">
        <li><strong>Create an optional username</strong><span>Only when you want to connect with another Money Plant user.</span></li>
        <li><strong>Choose a split to share</strong><span>Selected shared splits go to the service. Personal expenses and budgets stay local.</span></li>
        <li><strong>Sync when connected</strong><span>Changes wait on your device while offline and sync when a connection returns.</span></li>
      </ol>
      <p><strong>Custom people remain local.</strong> No username is needed to track a split manually.</p>
      <p class="planned-note">Optional device transfer is also planned. A local backup restores financial records; future online identity recovery will be a separate step.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
  <p class="privacy-footnote">Today, the app contacts GitHub to check for updates. That request does not include your financial records. Statements and payment links leave the app only when you choose to share or open them. <a class="text-link" href={`${base}/roadmap`}>Follow what’s growing →</a></p>
</div></section>
